---
description: What agents must not do in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

# Do not

- Widen types to make `tsc` pass (`any`, `unknown` bags, empty interfaces).
- Add a backend, router, new state library, or CSS framework unless the user asked.
- Mix default/named exports for views; ignore prop contracts; use `Math.random()` during render.
- Leave stubs (`Simplified for now`) or duplicate backward-compat fields.
- Put ESLint in npm scripts without installing ESLint and a config.
- Add Tailwind utilities while UI is SCSS modules; do not use unused packages (`tailwind-merge`).
- Expand scope (theme unlocks, camera capture, folder rewrite) while fixing types/logic.
- Commit secrets, photos, or backups. Do not amend/force-push/update git config unless asked.
- Silence or skip failing tests. Follow `AGENTS.md` when rules conflict with convenience.
